# Project layout

Keep new code under `src/` with these folders. Do not invent parallel trees.

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `src/cli/` | Typer CLI command handlers — **one command per file** |
| `src/hc_http/` | HTTP clients / request helpers (HC + PubMed), **by domain folder** |
| `src/pipeline/` | Ingestion, preprocessing, and orchestration steps only |
| `src/model/` | Pydantic models / schemas |
| `src/prompt/` | LLM prompt templates and static prompt markdown |
| `src/agents/` | Agents SDK agents — **one agent per subfolder** |
| `src/tools/` | Callable tools for agents — **by domain folder** wrapping `hc_http/` |
| `src/examples/` | Few-shot examples for prompts / agents |

```text
src/
  main.py                 # sole CLI entry (registers commands only)
  cli/
    <command>.py          # one Typer command per file
    http/                 # main.py http <domain> <command>
      fda/ ctg/ therapeutic_area/ pubmed/
  hc_http/                # HTTP clients by domain
    fda/ ctg/ therapeutic_area/ pubmed/
  pipeline/               # ingest / preprocess / run steps
  model/                  # pydantic only
  prompt/                 # prompts only
  agents/
    <agent_name>/         # one folder per agent
      ...
  tools/                  # agent tools by domain
    fda/ ctg/ therapeutic_area/ pubmed/
  examples/               # few-shot examples
```

## Rules

- Pipelines (ingestion, preprocessing, batch runs) live in `pipeline/`, not in `agents/`, `cli/`, or `main.py`.
- CLI argument parsing and `typer.echo` live in `cli/`; call into `pipeline/`, `agents/`, `hc_http/`, or `tools/` for real work.
- HTTP CLIs live under `src/cli/http/<domain>/` and are mounted as `main.py http <domain> <command>`.
- Group HC clients/tools by domain (`fda`, `ctg`, `therapeutic_area`, `pubmed`) rather than a flat `hc_http/` dump.
- Do not put Pydantic models in `pipeline/` or `agents/`; import from `model/`.
- Do not inline long prompts in agent code; load from `prompt/`.
- Do not bury few-shot examples in prompts as unstructured blobs when they belong in `examples/`.
- Reuse existing modules in these folders before adding new files.
- Do **not** name a top-level package `http` — it shadows the Python stdlib.
